+**The duration of the steps.** Each verification that runs a step of the
+adapter (`verify`, `verify --fast`, the CI) prints its duration at the end
+of its line, then the total. The total of the fast steps has a threshold,
+`[verify] fast_max_seconds`, 300 seconds by default: beyond five minutes
+of waiting, a sub-agent loses the cache of its conversation. When
+`verify --fast` runs them all and they pass, it keeps their total and the
+longest one in a local file, under `.socle/trace/`. Beyond the threshold,
+a warning, never a failure, gives the total, the threshold and the longest
+step with its duration: at the end of that run, on the line of a
+verification that does not run the steps again, and in the state, as long
+as the last complete run exceeds the threshold. A run where a step fails
+does not replace the previous one. The CI prints the durations, without a
+threshold: it runs on another machine. Lowering the threshold is free;
+raising it requires an approved request.
+
 **An adopted project** (installed with `--adoption`). The checks that
 failed on the existing code are named in `[adoption] warn_only`, and the
 findings present at installation in `[adoption.tolerated]`, per check,
